    "narrative": "Today\u2019s slate forces us to prioritize high-floor production as we navigate a relatively dense schedule. **Will Smith** remains our anchor at C1, boasting a score of 55.20. While the platoon matchup against Kerr is technically a slight negative, **Will Smith** benefits from a secure spot in the 3-hole and a robust xwOBA of .389, which keeps him firmly in the marginal-to-strong conversation. We are closely monitoring the lineup integrity of our speed-dependent assets, as **Masyn Winn**, **Justin Crawford**, and **Dylan Beavers** are expected to provide the necessary SB contributions that dictate our daily ceiling. Given the scarcity of SBs in this roster construction, these players are locked into the starting lineup regardless of marginal variations in projected efficiency.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the board was the exclusion of **Gavin Sheets**, who finished with a score of 39.92. He narrowly missed the \"Strong\" threshold, falling just short of the 40-point floor due to an unfavorable matchup against Henderson, whose 3.14 xERA effectively neutralized the platoon advantage **Gavin Sheets** typically provides against right-handed pitching. With **Cal Raleigh**, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, and **Lawrence Butler** currently inactive due to scheduled off-days, our bench depth is intentionally thin, forcing us to lean heavily on the remaining active roster. We are proceeding with caution regarding **Matt Chapman** and **Daulton Varsho**; both possess high-upside profiles, but their reliance on power in unfavorable park factors necessitates a disciplined approach to our remaining game caps. No major weather concerns have been flagged, but we are keeping a close watch on late-arriving lineup confirmations to ensure that high-OBP threats like **Luis Arraez** remain in optimal spots to drive in runs for **Bryce Harper**.",
